 - llama.cpp built from its releases `vX.Y.Z` (roadmap `release-0-3-1`): `build`'s `latest`, `build outdated` and `build update` take llama.cpp's newest weekly release, its nightly tags `b<N>`, pre-releases, being no release; a commit both forms tag, such as `b12359`, is built as `v1.0.0`; a release is built with `LLAMA_BUILD_IS_DEV=OFF`, so that `llama-server --version` prints its version, `1.0.0`, where a commit no release tags still prints `1.0.0-dev`, an option no installed build is compared with; an installed `b<N>` build keeps serving and passing `doctor`, reads as built from a commit, and `build update` builds the newest release beside it, `build use` going back to it; for such a build that cannot be read or is unlike its recipe, `doctor`, `up` and `gateway config` name `ai-ctl build llama.cpp`, since `--ref b<N>` would build another id.
 - The shipped inventory's budgets measured on the new builds: each chat and image model's `vram_mib` is its peak measured on 2026-11-14 with llama.cpp v1.0.0 and stable-diffusion.cpp `master-1098-b521db4` built with CUDA 13.5, no other process on the GPU but the desktop's — the 27B 21422 MiB and the 35B 19926, where their budgets were estimates, so that whisper large-v3-turbo now runs beside the 35B on a 24 GB GPU; FLUX.3 Image Klein 21909, Qwen-Image 2.1 23771 and Fibo 2.0 Dev 23859; an inventory an earlier `init` wrote keeps its budgets: copy them from `deploy/inventory.toml`.
 - audio.cpp v0.9.5, built with CUDA 13.5, the key's patch applying unchanged: the six audio.cpp models' `vram_mib` are their peaks measured on 2026-11-16 on that build — Qwen3-ASR 1.7B 5550 MiB, Qwen3-TTS 6902 and its `q8_0` 5530, Fish S2 Pro Q8_0 10084 and BF16 12610, Voxtral 4B TTS 8446 —, the cloning models with a reference of 38.56 s; they hold for v0.9.5, which `ai-ctl build update` builds, and an inventory an earlier `init` wrote keeps its budgets: copy them from `deploy/inventory.toml`.
+- A server no longer loads a library from the directory ai-ctl runs it in: builds are made with `CMAKE_BUILD_WITH_INSTALL_RPATH=ON` and `CMAKE_INSTALL_RPATH_USE_LINK_PATH=ON`, where CMake ended their `RUNPATH` with an empty element that glibc reads as the working directory, and `doctor` and `build`'s smoke test run each server in `/`, so that a `libgomp.so.1` another account left in `/tmp` no longer runs as the user when `doctor` runs there; a build made before keeps that element, and `ai-ctl build <project> --ref <id> --force` drops it.
 - llama-swap v273 (roadmap `release-0-3-1`): `gateway install` installs v273 and no other, checked against its pinned SHA-256; a request sent with `Expect: 100-continue`, as curl does for a body over about 1 MiB, such as an audio upload or an image edit, now gets the backend's own error status where v271 answered 200 with the error as its body (llama-swap #1319); `doctor` warns on v271, now behind the pin: run `ai-ctl gateway install`, then `ai-ctl down` and `ai-ctl up`, once after upgrading
 
