 through `/usr/local/cuda` once that toolkit is removed (`/etc/ld.so.conf.d/000_cuda.conf`): it
 keeps running after a minor change, and breaks when no toolkit of its major version is left.
+ai-ctl builds with `CMAKE_BUILD_WITH_INSTALL_RPATH=ON` and `CMAKE_INSTALL_RPATH_USE_LINK_PATH=ON`,
+so that the `RUNPATH` names that directory alone. A build made before 0.3.1 carries it padded
+with a trailing `:`, room CMake keeps for its rewrite at install, which ai-ctl never runs: glibc
+reads that empty element as the working directory, searched before the system's libraries, so
+such a build loads a `libgomp.so.1` or a `libc.so.6` it finds in the directory it runs in (CMake
+4.3.0 and glibc 2.43, 2026-11-18). `readelf -d <binary> | grep RUNPATH` shows it;
+`ai-ctl build <project> --ref <id> --force` drops it. `CMAKE_NO_BUILTIN_CHRPATH=ON`, CMake's
+other way, stops the Ninja generator at configure.
 
